<title>GERMANY: German grain trade seeks free mkt export rebates.</title>
<headline>German grain trade seeks free mkt export rebates.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids for the export of 5,000 tonnes of free market wheat with rebates in an 11.50 to 17.95 Ecus a tonne range, the state grain intervention board BLE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>BLE also received bids for the export of 69,000 tonnes of free market barley, where the desired restitutions were between 29.96 and 35.42 Ecus a tonne.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
